      "id": 1,
      "text": "Spring Valley sprang to life in 1884, founded to mine the rich coal beds of Northern Illinois.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Valley%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "By 1888, the town had exploded into a boom city called the “Magic City,” housing 3,000 residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Valley%2C_Illinois"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Spring Valley Historic Association opened its museum in 1977 inside the 1891 Old City Hall downtown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/8871"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Every October, residents celebrate the town’s past at the Spring Valley Historical Festival.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://museumsdatabase.com/museums/view/8871"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Before the city government existed, the Knights of Labor established a public library in 1885.",
